course: dictionary
lesson: 633
title: When a plan backfires
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A plan backfires when it goes wrong and gives the opposite of what you wanted, often hurting you instead. «Doing dares to be liked often backfires» means the dares make people like you less, not more.
explain: Look at the clues. Being liked is what the person wants, but people remember the silly thing, and a bigger dare digs the hole deeper. So backfire means going wrong in a way that hurts you.
explain: Use the swap test: put «went wrong» in place of «backfires» in «Playing one parent against the other usually causes more rows and backfires». It still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: Backfire can be a verb: backfire, backfires, backfired, backfiring.
fact: «The plan backfired» means the plan went wrong and hurt the person who made it.
fact: Backfire can also be a noun: a backfire is a sudden loud bang from a car or engine.
fact: In an engine, fuel explodes in the wrong place, and that makes the loud bang.
fact: Many fables show tricks and lies that backfire on the person who told them.
exercise: «Doing dares to be liked often backfires.» What does backfires mean here? | It works perfectly every time | *It goes wrong and has the opposite result to what you wanted | It wins a prize | It makes a loud bang
exercise: An old car engine backfires. What happens? | It slowly fills with paint | It turns into a bicycle | It goes quiet and smooth | *It makes a sudden loud bang
exercise: «Playing one parent against the other usually causes more rows and backfires.» What usually happens with this trick? | Your parents become happier | You get extra treats every time | The parents play a game together | *More rows, and the trick goes wrong
test: Sam says, «Lying to my teacher will backfire.» What does Sam mean? | Lying will make my teacher laugh | Lying will be easy to remember | Lying will make a loud bang | *Lying will go wrong and hurt me
test: In a car, what is a backfire? | A plan that goes wrong | *A sudden loud bang from the engine | A type of road | A kind of fuel
exam: «The plan backfired.» Which word could replace backfired without changing the meaning? | Grew bigger | Worked | Was forgotten | *Went wrong
